no one talks to me like that obviously  someone should it's been ten years since  Victoria Justice first starred in the  popular Nickelodeon series victorious  and long gone are the days when she was  booking successful TV shows like The  Suite Life of Zack &amp; Cody iCarly and  Zoey 101  unfortunately her career has quickly  fizzled join us as we take a deeper look  at Victoria Justice the dark side of her  Nickelodeon experience and its aftermath  that negatively impacted the direction  of her entire career Victoria Justice  grew up in Hollywood Florida and at the  age of 10 after landing a walk-on role  on the hit show Gilmore Girls the  aspiring actress and her parents made  the big move to the other Hollywood in  California in 2005 less than two years  after Victoria was accepted into the  musical theatre program at the Milliken  Performing Arts Academy in Los Angeles  during that time she even appeared in  advertisements for Ralph Lauren guests  gap and yes even peanut butter toast  crunch cereal that same year she was  booking acting jobs on such shows as The  Suite Life of Zack and Cody as well as a  reoccurring role on the Nickelodeon TV  show zoey 101  soon after the show's creator dan  schneider was so impressed with the  talented young star that he created a  leading role for her in her very own  show the one we all know and love  victorious you could say the Victoria  was quickly making her way up the acting  ladder and was making a substantial mark  in the entertainment world things were  moving quickly and Victoria's career was  taking off you know you're actually not  terrible things were going extremely  well for Victoria and her acting career  she even began building her singing  career due to the huge success of her  hit TV show however after three seasons  of victorious everything came to an  unexpected end the show was abruptly  canceled in 2013 and it didn't even get  a proper finale episode there was so  much mystery around it ending and  there's much speculation as to why one  of the biggest accusations was that  Victoria wanted to leave the show to  focus on her singing career and was in  fact going off to do a solo tour after  the last season  others blamed Victoria's co-star ariana  grande because she was about to star in  her own spin-off series salmon cat a lot  of tension surrounded the accusations  and fans were angry with Ariana but she  quickly crushed the rumors that it  wasn't her fault she instead blamed  Victoria in a response in her ask.fm  account saying the only reason  victorious ended is because one girl  didn't want to do it  Toria responded on Twitter saying some  people would throw someone that they  consider a friend under the bus just to  make themselves look good  hashtag stop being a phony hashtag if  they only knew  yikes so much drama another unfortunate  realization of the show was that  although it was very popular and its  viewership was reaching two million  viewers on average the show failed to  create hit songs  unlike other popular shows such as Glee  who had a whopping 207 hit songs  throughout at six seasons the show's  victorious album hit number five on the  top 200 billboard list but only sold  40,000 copies it's quite possible that  because the show didn't feature charting  music that Nickelodeon didn't see it  making enough substantial profits from  the show so they decided to cancel it as  successful as the show was turns out  parents hated it many complains that the  parents in the show were portrayed as  pushovers and that the show represented  a false reality of the average teenage  girl they also complained that the show  lacked diversity another odd fact about  victorious was that it had a very strict  rule surrounding the actresses  hairstyles the show's creator Dan  Schneider implemented the rule that all  girls on the show must swear their hair  down he even revealed in his Dan Warp  blog as everyone who works for me knows  I almost never let girls wear ponytails  on my shows only once do we see Victoria  in a ponytail during the scene where she  has to pick up a huge mess Snyder said  it was necessary for that scene because  of the large mess the character would  have to clean up and that's why her hair  is in a ponytail  one of the biggest and darkest  controversies to come out of Victoria's  experience on the show was her feud with  ariana grande and the show was cancelled  there was quite a lot of finger-pointing  in regards to who was to blame for its  ending and to further the tension and  add fuel to the feud an interview  article in Seventeen magazine with  ariana grande had quoted her saying I  worked with someone who told me they'd  never like me but for some reason I just  felt like I needed her approval  so I started changing myself to please  her it made me stop being social and  friendly I was so unhappy many suspected  that Ari was referring to her victorious  co-star however Victoria two years later  on the Meredith Vieira show had  explained you know how the media like  twist words I was not talking about you  obviously like I was talking about one  of someone on Broadway  sadly once the thought was put out there  it's hard to make it go away no matter  how many photo ops and even reunions you  do fans have been speculating for years  since the show ended that there was  definitely a feud between them in April  2015  Victoria when asked if she would ever  work with Ariana again was quoted as  saying I think we're kind of both on our  separate paths right now I've been more  focused on acting and she's doing her  singing thing and doing awesome  many contemplated that it was blessed to  do with different career paths and more  to do with their dislike for each other  it didn't help that several years after  that in 2018 ariana released a video for  her song thank you next and although it  features several members from the cast  of Victorious such as daniella monet  Matt Bennett and Liz Gillies justice was  nowhere to be seen further fueling the  feud theories about the two girls after  having to leave Coachella early in 2019  fans assume Victoria was avoiding ariana  by leaving the event right before  Grande's performance Victoria quickly  responded with the video clearing up any  confusion that she bailed because she  didn't want to see her friends perform  and although at the time it went  unnoticed the feud between Victoria and  Ariana caused an old video from 2010 to  resurface Victoria was accused of being  jealous of Ariana receiving compliments  over her beautiful voice and how she is  always singing on set when all the girls  in the video were talking about  they love to sing Victoria added that  brings us to April 2020 doing a zoom  video call for the show's cast ten year  reunion a viewer commented I think we  are all the best in reference to that  same video from 10 years prior  Ariana's shot down the commenter  immediately squashing any resurfacing of  those old feud rumors so maybe there  isn't a feud but maybe there is we might  never know  unfortunately for Victoria it has only  continued the speculation and gossip  about anything she does that happens to  be connected to Arianna it's something  that she will never be able to escape  sadly even if her in Ariana's feud is  not true a fictional notion that justice  is mean and difficult to work with has  hurt her reputation and career that  brings us to Victoria's failing career  since her time on victorious victorious  is a beautiful talented actress and once  starred as the lead in her own TV show  so why did her career seem to tank after  victorious was cancelled it obviously  isn't due to lack of talent as justice  is a triple threat talented in acting  singing and dancing you would think she  would be unstoppable booking hit roll  after roll but her career has gone  nowhere  sadly Victoria just can't seem to make  anything stick since victorious after  leaving the show she set out on building  her music career and her first debut  song gold never made it to the top 100  billboard lists nor did it see much in  sales her album only sold a mere 30,000  copies Victoria left her label with  Columbia Records and decided to focus on  her acting career her first big movie  after victorious called fun-sized tanked  from there she was only able to acquire  small roles in shows like man with the  plan  Queen America an American housewife  eventually Victoria was able to land a  leading role in the TV show I candy but  it was cancelled after one season she  also starred as Janet in the TV movie  Rocky Horror Picture Show back in 2016  but the movie also flopped only getting  a 25% rating on Rotten Tomatoes  it seems lately her choice of film and  television shows are much darker and  more adults than we are used to seeing  her in like eye candy or 50 states of  fright there are much different types of  characters than her original role as  Tori Vega in victorious perhaps her  fanbase has trouble seeing her in any  other way and she unfortunately is  suffering from the typecasting curse  unfortunately it makes me so sad there  is speculation that her failing career  is due to the fact that she lacks brand  and her persona is somewhat boring she  has sort of a plain Jane vibe about her  and in an industry where image is  everything and you need to constantly  stand out amongst the crowd her sweet  teeny bopper persona no longer serves  her in her career she is often mistaken  for Nina Dobrev not to mention compared  to several other celebrities which in  some ways is seen as a huge compliment  of the actress but it also is a  deterrent in the casting room casting  directors are always looking for someone  who stands out from the rest  unfortunately it's easy for them to  choose another actress over her what's  the worst thing you've ever done I  squirted hot cheese over my friend and  her current boyfriend  with all these unlucky career flops we  wonder how Victoria was able to snatch  the hosting job for the upcoming Kids  Choice Awards with someone who is hardly  ever in the spotlight it does seem odd  to give her the hosting gig however  interestingly enough the original  broadcast of the first episode of  Victorious took place following the Kids  Choice Awards back in 2010 we wonder if  there is something in the works that  will be announced on the awards show  seeing as it is the 10-year reunion of  victorious perhaps a reboot or an  entirely new show featuring Victoria  Justice the fact that she was chosen to  host the award show tells us that she  hasn't completely lost her popularity  amongst teens otherwise she would never  have been picked in the first place her  job as host will definitely bring her to  the online forefront of viewers and fans  alike creating more and better  opportunities for her in the future the  awards show will be airing live via the  internet a first for any award show  since the corona virus pandemic the show  was originally set up to be hosted by  chance the rapper but now has Victoria  to take the reins for whatever reason  you may think Victoria's career has  flopped or at least fizzled we can't  help but think her negative experience  on Victorious was a huge cause of her  downfall  from feuds and constant gossip it's easy  to peg Victoria as difficult to work  with  we hope her hosting duties will help  boost her career in a better more  positive direction and she finally  starts to see the success she has been  working so hard to achieve what do you  think was Victoria's Nickelodeon  experience really that dark she  definitely had to endure some difficulty  surrounding the show but more so since  her days as a Nickelodeon star with a  career that seems to have flopped we'll  see what happens to her new hosting gig  in May 20-22 you think she'll do a good  job let us know in the comments below

